---
import PirschScript from '@fresh.codes/astro-pirsch-proxy/components/PirschScript.astro'
---

<html lang='en'>
  <head>
    <meta charset='utf-8' />
    <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1' />
    <title>Tags Example - Astro Pirsch Proxy</title>
    <PirschScript
      data-tag-author='John Doe'
      data-tag-category='tutorial'
      data-tag='analytics,privacy'
    />
    <style>
      body {
        font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
        max-width: 800px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 2rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      a {
        color: #4338ca;
        text-decoration: none;
      }
      a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }
      .info {
        background: #f3f4f6;
        padding: 1rem;
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        margin: 1rem 0;
      }
      code {
        background: #e5e7eb;
        padding: 0.125rem 0.25rem;
        border-radius: 0.25rem;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
      }
      pre {
        background: #1f2937;
        color: #f3f4f6;
        padding: 1rem;
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
      }
      button {
        background: #4338ca;
        color: white;
        border: none;
        padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
        border-radius: 0.25rem;
        cursor: pointer;
        font-size: 1rem;
        margin: 0.5rem 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
      }
      button:hover {
        background: #3730a3;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p><a href='/'>← Back to Examples</a></p>

    <h1>Tags Example</h1>

    <div class='info'>
      <p>
        <strong>What are tags?</strong> Tags allow you to segment your analytics data
        by custom attributes like author, category, content type, etc.
      </p>
      <p>This page demonstrates three types of tags:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>data-tag-author="John Doe"</code> - Custom tag with a value
        </li>
        <li><code>data-tag-category="tutorial"</code> - Another custom tag</li>
        <li>
          <code>data-tag="analytics,privacy"</code> - Comma-separated list of tags
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>How Tags Work</h2>
    <p>
      When you add data attributes to the Pirsch script, they're automatically
      included with every page view and event tracked on this page.
    </p>

    <h3>Script Configuration</h3>
    <pre>&lt;PirschScript
  data-tag-author="John Doe"
  data-tag-category="tutorial"
  data-tag="analytics,privacy"
/&gt;</pre>

    <h3>Use Cases for Tags</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Blog posts:</strong> Track by author, category, or series</li>
      <li>
        <strong>E-commerce:</strong> Track by product category, brand, or price range
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Documentation:</strong> Track by section, difficulty level, or topic
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Landing pages:</strong> Track by campaign, source, or variant
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class='info'>
      <h3>Verify in Pirsch Dashboard</h3>
      <p>
        In your Pirsch dashboard, you can filter and segment your analytics by
        these tags. Check the Tags section to see:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>author: John Doe</li>
        <li>category: tutorial</li>
        <li>tag: analytics</li>
        <li>tag: privacy</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Test Custom Event</h2>
    <p>Click the button below to send a custom event to Pirsch:</p>
    <button id='btn-event'>Send Test Event</button>

    <p><a href='/'>← Back to Examples</a></p>

    <script is:inline>
      document.getElementById('btn-event')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (window.pirsch) {
          window.pirsch('Button Click Test', {
            meta: {
              page: 'index',
              action: 'test-event',
            },
          })
          alert('Test event sent! Check the Network tab to see the request.')
        } else {
          alert(
            'Pirsch script not loaded yet. Please wait a moment and try again.',
          )
        }
      })
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
